/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 158 0 R
/T (The Internet is a network of networks. It connects many smaller networks, such as home networks, school networks, business networks, and data centers. Together, these networks allow billions of devices to communicate. People use the Internet for messaging, video calls, streaming, gaming, research, shopping, and learning. Businesses, schools, and governments also rely on it every day. The Internet makes communication and access to information fast and widespread.)
