/Title (A NETWORK IS A GROUP OF CONNECTED COMPUTING DEVICES. THESE DEVICES CAN INCLUDE PHONES, COMPUTERS, TABLETS, SERVERS, AND PRINTERS. SOME DEVICES MAINLY SEND AND RECEIVE DATA, WHILE OTHERS HELP MOVE DATA THROUGH THE NETWORK. EVERY DEVICE CONNECTED TO A NETWORK PLAYS A ROLE. SOME DEVICES ARE USED BY PEOPLE DIRECTLY, LIKE PHONES AND LAPTOPS. OTHERS, LIKE SERVERS, STORE AND PROVIDE INFORMATION. DEVICES SUCH AS ROUTERS HELP MOVE DATA THROUGH THE NETWORK SO COMMUNICATION CAN HAPPEN.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 765 0 R
>>
