/Title (Data sent over the Internet is broken into small pieces called packets. This is called packet switching. Each packet carries part of the data, along with information about where it came from and where it is going. At the destination, the packets are put back together in the correct order. Packet switching helps the Internet work efficiently because many users can share the network at the same time, and packets can be rerouted if one path is busy or unavailable.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 814 0 R
>>
endobj
